From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 21:23:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02190/11362] [outer-loop] verifier-routed search stage in the
 ARC solver harness (north-star efficiency loop)

OfflineSolver now takes an optional verifier (an energy/goal-distance on the
state, lower=closer-to-win) and runs best-first ordered by it; verifier=None
degrades to BFS. DEMONSTRATED on lp85: same L3 reached, plain BFS 3860 states vs
verifier-routed 359 -> 10.75x fewer states expanded. The verifier is pluggable
(computed now, LEARNED next), closing the loop from recipe-routing to the search
itself being verifier-pruned -- the project's verifier-moat thesis applied to ARC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
